  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 7% permanent failure cap, which keeps Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) on the market, while customers get numeric per-model rates and the public is spared them. S5 makes an 8-per-100k mandatory recall with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) to recall, and S3 combines a 36-month new-unit shut-off start with a 6-year retrofit window that favours Northwind's lower 38% shut-off coverage. S1 is the strongest section, with 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, which closes the unreported-incident gap for both companies."
 },
